# This file has to survive a Windows checkout itself. core.autocrlf would
# otherwise write it with CRLF, and a stray CR riding along at the end of a
# pattern is a pattern that stops matching.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Flutter rewrites the plugin registration files on every build, and writes them
# with LF. Without this, core.autocrlf expects CRLF in the working tree, so every
# build leaves one of these looking modified while its bytes are identical to
# what is committed -- noise that hides the one build that really did change
# something, which is when a plugin has been added or removed. The pattern
# covers every platform directory, so adding one does not mean remembering to
# add its copy of this rule.
*/flutter/generated_* text eol=lf
